        {"q": "Where can you report after you stop contact?", "choices": ["Only by replying to the sender.", "ReportFraud.ftc.gov, IC3, and VA’s fraud channels, using addresses you look up yourself.", "By posting your Social Security number so others can check the story.", "By paying a recovery fee to the same caller."], "answer": 1, "why": "Those are the public reporting doors. A link inside the suspicious message is not one of them. Do not pay the same party to recover the money.", "source": FTC_REPORT, "sourceName": "FTC ReportFraud"},
        {"q": "A low concern score in Scam Guardian means:", "choices": ["The message is safe to pay.", "The written rules did not see much. It can still be a scam.", "VA has reviewed the sender.", "The picture was proven real."], "answer": 1, "why": "The tool shows rule matches. Absence of a rule is not a clearance, and the page does not inspect whether a voice or video is synthetic.", "source": IC3_GAI, "sourceName": "FBI IC3 PSA I-120324-PSA"}
