        {"q": "What can this toolkit tell you about a video that looks like an officer demanding payment?", "choices": ["Whether the video is a deepfake.", "Nothing reliable about the pixels. Treat the payment demand as suspicious even without a detector.", "The speaker’s real unit.", "A certainty score for the voice."], "answer": 1, "why": "No face, voice, or video detector is included. IC3 says identification is difficult. The safe step is to verify through a channel you already trust and not to pay from the video.", "source": IC3_GAI, "sourceName": "FBI IC3 PSA I-120324-PSA"},
        {"q": "A caller sounds like your grandchild and wants money now. What do the FTC and the FBI say to do?", "choices": ["Trust the voice if it sounds emotional.", "Hang up and call the person back on a number you know is theirs. A family code word, agreed in advance, can help.", "Buy gift cards and read the numbers if the voice cries.", "Stay on the line while you get the cards."], "answer": 1, "why": "The FTC family-emergency alert and the FBI generative-AI alert both say not to trust the voice and to verify on a known number. Gift cards, wires, and crypto are warning signs.", "source": FTC_FAMILY, "sourceName": "FTC family-emergency alert"},
        {"q": "Spotting a visual glitch, such as strange hands, is:", "choices": ["A complete test that clears the video if you see no glitch.", "An optional clue. It is not a reliable clearance, and you do not need it in order to hang up.", "The score Scam Guardian prints.", "Required before you may contact IC3."], "answer": 1, "why": "IC3 lists imperfections you can look for and also says synthetic content can be hard to identify. Do not send money because an image looked fine.", "source": IC3_GAI, "sourceName": "FBI IC3 PSA I-120324-PSA"},
        {"q": "Creating synthetic media is:", "choices": ["Always a federal crime by itself, according to the FBI alert.", "Not inherently illegal. Using it to defraud or extort someone is the harm the FBI describes.", "Proof this toolkit failed.", "Something VA asks claimants to do."], "answer": 1, "why": "IC3 says creation or distribution of synthetic content is not inherently illegal, and that the content can be used to commit fraud and extortion. This lesson is not legal advice about a specific video.", "source": IC3_GAI, "sourceName": "FBI IC3 PSA I-120324-PSA"},
        {"q": "Limiting public clips of your voice and face:", "choices": ["Makes every future scam impossible.", "Reduces material a stranger can copy. It does not stop every scam.", "Is required by this toolkit’s license.", "Replaces multi-factor authentication."], "answer": 1, "why": "IC3 suggests limiting public image and voice and making accounts private. That is a reduction in raw material, not a guarantee. CISA’s sheet is about organizational preparation, not a promise of personal detection.", "source": IC3_GAI, "sourceName": "FBI IC3 PSA I-120324-PSA"}
